WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:02.922
I expand the Duplication section to read

00:02.922 --> 00:05.545
the project total. Deslop shows how many

00:05.545 --> 00:08.167
lines it analysed and how many it

00:08.167 --> 00:10.790
found in repeated code. The percentage describes

00:10.790 --> 00:13.412
those files; it does not tell me

00:13.412 --> 00:15.660
that a cleanup is automatically safe.

00:16.460 --> 00:18.673
I open the file rows behind that

00:18.673 --> 00:20.885
total and inspect the highlighted code. This

00:20.885 --> 00:23.098
lets me connect the number to real

00:23.098 --> 00:25.311
source lines. When I review a result,

00:25.311 --> 00:27.523
I want to understand which files were

00:27.523 --> 00:29.420
checked and what work was counted.

00:30.220 --> 00:32.353
Next I put the reported copies side

00:32.353 --> 00:34.487
by side. I check that they really

00:34.487 --> 00:36.620
repeat the same work and look at

00:36.620 --> 00:38.753
their differences. This is the evidence I

00:38.753 --> 00:40.887
use to decide what deserves attention, rather

00:40.887 --> 00:43.020
than treating a percentage as a verdict.

00:43.820 --> 00:46.125
I exclude a folder in the settings

00:46.125 --> 00:48.430
file and save it. The sidebar updates

00:48.430 --> 00:50.735
because those files are no longer part

00:50.735 --> 00:53.040
of the analysis. Before comparing two results,

00:53.040 --> 00:55.346
I check settings like this so I

00:55.346 --> 00:57.651
know that both runs measured the same

00:57.651 --> 00:57.980
files.
